From 5e528f85d6fab4b2b25c3d5b23ef2b35117f3ff0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ElixirOffice contributors <noreply@elixiroffice.org>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 20:49:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(word): picture bullets are read, drawn and written back

A list level can have a picture for a bullet: the numbering keeps a
table of them, read from and written to the binary format (core 0203),
the level its picture's id, and the bullet is drawn as the picture, at
Word's size, where a text bullet was drawn.

From ElixirOffice's sdkjs, commit de6ba67 (their 0.7.2), the part of it
that answers their issue #66's picture bullets, with two changes of ours.
A level's id goes in the change log after IsLgl, which was a byte of 0
or 1 ending the level; its bit 1 now says an id follows, where theirs
appended an id to every level, so that a change log written before,
recovered by a newer build, still reads. And x2t's renderer, which
prints and exports to PDF, has no image loader to ask for the picture:
it draws it from its address, as it does every other picture.
